    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by the dual-threat potential of **Cole Carrigg** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, our two most potent offensive options. **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Lugo, S and a substantial park factor boost that vaults his efficiency well above the base projection. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (80.22) remains a locked-in core piece, capitalizing on a strong matchup against the lefty Liberatore; the high-leverage spot in the batting order, combined with favorable platoon splits, makes him our highest-projected source of counting stats for the day. **Gunnar Henderson** (68.30) also warrants attention; despite facing the tough arm of Wheeler, the extreme park factor and his spot in the #3 hole keep his efficiency high, though we must monitor the risk of his high-strikeout profile against elite velocity.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Luis Lara** (50.28). While his metrics are respectable, he narrowly missed the starting cut because our outfield depth\u2014led by the high-upside pairing of **Jackson Merrill** (63.41) and **Andy Pages** (63.49)\u2014offers a more efficient path to 5x5 production today. **Andy Pages** is particularly intriguing; his ability to exploit a slow pitcher delivery profile, alongside **Kyle Tucker** (64.50), provides us with much-needed volatility and steal potential. We have effectively benched **Wade Meckler** (38.41) and **Denzer Guzman** (31.85) to preserve our game caps, as both struggle against the high-skill arm of Misiorowski, falling well below our 40.0 efficiency floor. \n\nManagers should remain alert regarding **Liam Hicks** (59.93) and **Drake Baldwin** (51.79); while both are starting, the catching position remains a volatile spot in our rotation. We are banking on **Nasim Nunez** (64.28) to provide efficient production from the bottom of the order against Ritchie, relying on his speed to mitigate his lower batting position. There are no immediate weather threats to report, but with several hitters facing starters with xERA marks flirting with the 4.00\u20135.00 range, we are positioned for a high-volume scoring day, provided **Luis Robert Jr.** (50.58) can overcome his difficult platoon matchup against Alcantara, S.",
